From: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 12:10:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] AML: read the hvcC length size as the converter does

The HEVC latches walk the demux payload as length-prefixed NALs when the
stream's extradata is an hvcC record, and as Annex-B otherwise. The
length size was read only for a version 1 record, while
CBitstreamConverter takes as hvcC any extradata of 23 bytes or more that
does not start with 00 00 00 or 00 00 01, version 0 included (the draft
14496-15 layout some muxers still write). Such a stream was then
scanned as Annex-B, where a start code pattern inside a length-prefixed
NAL could pass for a NAL of its own, and its RPU and SEI were missed.

The size is now read when the converter opens, which for HEVC into
Annex-B it does on exactly that test.

Signed-off-by: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>

diff --git a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDCodecs/Video/DVDVideoCodecAmlogic.cpp b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDCodecs/Video/DVDVideoCodecAmlogic.cpp
index 8321ee4..e951c46 100644
--- a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDCodecs/Video/DVDVideoCodecAmlogic.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDCodecs/Video/DVDVideoCodecAmlogic.cpp
@@ -359,11 +359,10 @@ bool CDVDVideoCodecAmlogic::Open(CDVDStreamInfo &hints, CDVDCodecOptions &option
       }
       m_pFormatName = "am-h265";
       m_bitstream = new CBitstreamConverter();
-      m_bitstream->Open(m_hints.codec, m_hints.extradata.GetData(), m_hints.extradata.GetSize(), true);
-
-      // length-prefix size from the original hvcC, read before the extradata
-      // below becomes Annex-B. Stays 0 for Annex-B input
-      if (m_hints.extradata.GetSize() > 21 && m_hints.extradata.GetData()[0] == 1)
+      // it opens on hvcC extradata only; the length-prefix size is read before the extradata
+      // below becomes Annex-B, and stays 0 for Annex-B input
+      if (m_bitstream->Open(m_hints.codec, m_hints.extradata.GetData(),
+                            m_hints.extradata.GetSize(), true))
         m_nalLengthSize = (m_hints.extradata.GetData()[21] & 0x3) + 1;
 
       // check for hevc-hvcC and convert to h265-annex-b
